        "y": "1071",
        "width": "380",
        "height": "197",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "START MODERATE\nGroup exercises at full dose and progressive strengthening within the pain rules. Full core battery."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7810",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:7810",
        "x": "1100",
        "y": "941",
        "connectorStart": "1:6807",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:6819",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "LS4-1b&gt;LS4-MD"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:6823",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:6823",
        "x": "1360",
        "y": "1071",
        "width": "380",
        "height": "197",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "START STRONGER\nCore programme loading, lifting and carrying practice, return to sport or heavy work tasks. Full core battery."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7814",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:7814",
        "x": "1550",
        "y": "941",
        "connectorStart": "1:6811",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:6823",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "LS4-1c&gt;LS4-LO"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:6827",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:6827",
        "x": "720",
        "y": "1403",
        "width": "760",
        "height": "324",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "LS4-2 · STarT Back screening tool (9 questions, about 2 minutes)\nScores the risk of a poor outcome from yellow flags and spreading pain. Total 0–3 = LOW risk; total 4 or more → look at the 5 psychological items: 3 or less = MEDIUM, 4–5 = HIGH (Hill 2008).\n• LOW: advice, reassurance, the group’s exercises at home; 1–2 contacts.\n• MEDIUM: a physiotherapy-led exercise programme (about 6 sessions).\n• HIGH: psychologically informed physiotherapy — tackle fears and beliefs, graded exposure, pacing, goal-setting; involve a counsellor or doctor for low mood.\nStratified care improved disability at 4 and 12 months and saved costs compared with usual best care (Hill 2011, 851 patients)."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7826",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:7826",
        "x": "1100",
        "y": "1274",
        "connectorStart": "1:6823",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:6827",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "LS4-LO&gt;LS4-2"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7822",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:7822",
        "x": "1100",
        "y": "1274",
        "connectorStart": "1:6819",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:6827",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "LS4-MD&gt;LS4-2"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7818",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:7818",
        "x": "650",
        "y": "1299",
        "connectorStart": "1:6815",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:6827",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "LS4-HI&gt;LS4-2"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:6831",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:6831",
        "x": "120",
        "y": "1837",
        "width": "680",
        "height": "604",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "LS4-3 · CORE BASELINE BATTERY (about 10 minutes)\nNeeds: a chair, a stopwatch, 10 m of floor and a phone. Repeat the SAME set at week 0, 4 and 12.\n1. Pain 0–10 (faces version for low literacy): average and worst in the last week; leg pain scored separately if present.\n2. Patient-Specific Functional Scale (PSFS): the patient names their 3 hardest tasks and rates each 0–10 — this becomes the goal list. Prompt with local tasks: floor sitting and rising, squatting toilet, bending to sweep or wash clothes, carrying water or head-loads, field work, riding a two-wheeler, lifting a child.\n3. Disability questionnaire: Roland-Morris (24 items) or the Oswestry Disability Index — check for a validated Hindi or Marathi version.\n4. Body chart: where the symptoms reach — watch for centralisation across visits.\n5. Movement: fingertip-to-floor distance bending forward; arching back (painful? how far?).\n6. 5 × sit-to-stand (seconds) or the 30-second chair stand.\n7. 10 m fast walk (seconds); for stenosis, time or distance until symptoms start.\n8. Trunk endurance: side-bridge hold time each side (physio-level).\n9. Nerve check if any leg symptoms: heel and toe walking, SLR angle.\nMEANINGFUL CHANGE: about 30% improvement from baseline on pain or disability scores (Ostelo 2008)."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7830",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:7830",
        "x": "460",
        "y": "1733",
        "connectorStart": "1:6827",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:6831",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "LS4-2&gt;LS4-3"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:6835",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:6835",
        "x": "870",
        "y": "1837",
        "width": "680",
        "height": "485",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "LS4-4 · ADD-ON MODULE — pick the one that matches the working diagnosis\nBack module (LD1–LD5, LD9): Oswestry or Roland-Morris; repeated-movement response; side-bridge time.\nSciatica module (LD6, LD7): leg pain 0–10 apart from back pain; SLR angle; nerve screen at every visit (any new weakness → L5).\nStenosis module (LD8): walking time or distance to symptom onset and maximum; Zurich Claudication Questionnaire; Timed Up-and-Go; Romberg.\nPelvic girdle module (LD10): Pelvic Girdle Questionnaire; active straight-leg raise score 0–10.\nYellow-flag module (LD5, LD11, or STarT Back HIGH): STarT Back; Fear-Avoidance Beliefs Questionnaire or Tampa Scale; PHQ-9 mood screen → doctor if moderate or worse; sleep.\nBone-health module (LD12): height to the millimetre at each visit; back-of-head-to-wall distance; Timed Up-and-Go; falls in the last year."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7834",
      "type": "connector",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:7834",
        "x": "1100",
        "y": "1733",
        "connectorStart": "1:6827",
        "connectorStartCap": "NONE",
        "connectorEnd": "1:6835",
        "connectorEndCap": "ARROW_LINES"
      },
      "text": "LS4-2&gt;LS4-4"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:6839",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:6839",
        "x": "1620",
        "y": "1837",
        "width": "460",
        "height": "324",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "PAIN RULES FOR HOME EXERCISE\n• Pain up to about 5 out of 10 during exercise is acceptable if it has settled back to its usual level by the next morning. If not, hold or step down one level.\n• Centralisation rule: symptoms moving toward the spine = good; spreading further down the leg = stop that exercise.\n• Any new numbness, weakness, or bladder or bowel change → stop and re-run Stage 1."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:6843",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:6843",
        "x": "840",
        "y": "2551",
        "width": "520",
        "height": "197",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "LS4-5 · WEEK 1 — dose check\nASK: “Did the pain settle back to normal by the next morning after exercising? Has the leg pain moved up toward the back, or further down?”"
    },
